fuxi: 0110 -- a UDP command channel, so the phone can be restarted over USB

The console streams one way (5140).  This is the other way, on UDP 5141, which
turns the bring-up loop from "walk over and hold the keys" into one datagram.

  help | stat | cpu | echo <text> | restart

Why UDP and not the 0x88B5 frames from 0106: those need AF_PACKET, i.e. root on
the host.  A datagram to 192.168.7.2:5141 from an unprivileged socket is enough,
which is what makes the loop scriptable.

The listener binds INADDR_ANY on purpose -- the address arrives later via
SIOCAIFADDR and it has to be listening before that -- and reopens the socket
after a failure instead of giving up, so a link that is up before the interface
address exists still works once it appears.

"restart" answers first, waits a tick so the datagram leaves, then calls
PEHaltRestart(kPERestartCPU): a reset out of the kernel, not through userspace.
It lands in whatever the boot partition holds (Android), where the host can
'adb reboot bootloader' and boot the next image.

Harness: applied=109 skipped=0.
